  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "tag": "Claude Code",
      "heading": "Claude Code just got *mods*",
      "subheading": "What's new, how they work, and the catch",
      "chapter": "What's new",
      "narration": "Claude Code just got mods: you can change how it behaves and what it draws on screen. But it already had hooks, skills and MCP. So what's actually new? Let's build it up from the simplest picture.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "Claude Code",
          "icon": "code",
          "at": "Claude Code just got"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mods",
          "icon": "lambda",
          "at": "change how it behaves",
          "sfx": "impact"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hooks · Skills · MCP",
          "icon": "worker",
          "at": "it already had"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "at": "actually new"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "The agent loop",
      "chapter": "The agent loop",
      "narration": "Start with the loop you already know. You type a prompt, and Claude Code sends it to the model. The model answers with a tool call, like running a command or editing a file, and Claude Code runs it on your machine.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "You type a prompt",
          "show": [
            "you",
            "cc"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "you",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "prompt",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "sends it to",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "model",
            "label": "prompt",
            "color": "blue"
          },
          "status": {
            "model": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "answers with a tool call",
          "packet": {
            "from": "model",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "tool call",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "model": "idle"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "Claude Code runs it",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "machine",
            "label": "run · edit",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "machine": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "on your machine",
          "camera": [],
          "note": {
            "text": "Prompt → model → *tool call* → your machine",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Extensions, from the outside",
      "chapter": "Skills, MCP and settings hooks",
      "narration": "Until now, you extended it from the outside. A skill is instructions Claude reads. An MCP server is an outside program that gives Claude new tools. And a settings hook runs your script when something happens, like right before a tool call.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "from the outside",
          "status": {
            "machine": "idle"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "A skill is",
          "show": [
            "skill"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "skill",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "SKILL.md",
            "color": "gray"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "Skill = *instructions*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "An MCP server",
          "show": [
            "mcp"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "mcp",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "new tools",
            "color": "teal"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "MCP = *new tools*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "a settings hook",
          "show": [
            "hook"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Settings hook = *your script*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "before a tool call",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "hook",
            "label": "tool call?",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "hook": "busy"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "A narrow door",
      "narration": "Each one talks to Claude Code through a narrow door. A script can say yes or no to a tool call, or change its input. But it can't draw a panel, change the spinner, or take over a command. That's the gap.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "a narrow door",
          "focus": [
            "skill",
            "mcp",
            "hook",
            "cc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "yes or no",
          "packet": {
            "from": "hook",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "yes / no",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "hook": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "change its input",
          "note": {
            "text": "Outside: *allow · block · edit input*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "can't draw a panel",
          "focus": [
            "cc"
          ],
          "status": {
            "hook": "idle"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "Can't *draw* or *take over*",
            "tone": "bad"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "That's the gap",
          "focus": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "text": "Inside",
      "caption": "a mod's code runs in Claude Code's own process",
      "tone": "info",
      "icon": "lambda",
      "sfx": "impact",
      "chapter": "Mods: code inside Claude Code",
      "narration": "So, what if your code could run inside Claude Code itself?"
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "What a mod is",
      "narration": "That's a mod. It's a plugin with JavaScript or TypeScript functions, and Claude Code calls them when something happens: a tool call, a prompt you send, or a piece of the screen being drawn.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "That's a mod",
          "show": [
            "mod"
          ],
          "focus": [
            "cc",
            "mod"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Mod = *functions inside* Claude Code",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "a tool call",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "mod",
            "label": "tool.call",
            "color": "yellow"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "a prompt you send",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "mod",
            "label": "prompt",
            "color": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "being drawn",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cc",
            "to": "mod",
            "label": "ui.render",
            "color": "purple"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Observe, rewrite, or answer",
      "narration": "The function runs before Claude Code acts, so it decides what happens next. It can just watch. It can rewrite the event. Or it can answer it itself, so the usual behavior never runs.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "runs before Claude Code",
          "status": {
            "mod": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "just watch",
          "packet": {
            "from": "mod",
            "to": "cc",
            "label": "pass",
            "color": "gray"
